        You can appeal a Medicare IRMAA surcharge if you experienced a qualifying <strong class="irmaa-gold">Life-Changing Event</strong> — retirement, work reduction, divorce, spousal death, or pension loss — that caused your current income to drop below what Social Security used to set your surcharge. File <strong class="irmaa-gold">SSA Form SSA-44</strong> with documentation of the event within 60 days of your IRMAA notice. If approved, your Medicare premium is reduced immediately.
      </p>
    </div>

